WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  america  once again engulfed in anger after  police  opened fire on a black man  a video on social media appears to show  a man trying to get into his car  before he's shot in the back  he's been identified as jacob blake and  was taken to hospital in a serious  condition  his fiancee says his three children were  in the car at the time  you shot him numerous times for no  reason it didn't take all that  disregard that my kids was in the car at  all and you knew they was in there  because i kept screaming it before y'all  even made it to the other side of the  driver's side  to get him in the car i've been yelling  at the whole time  wisconsin's governor has also responded  with a strongly worded statement  saying while we do not have all the  details yet what we know for certain  is that he is not the first black man or  person to have been shot or injured or  mercilessly  killed at the hands of individuals in  law enforcement in our state or country  the kenosha professional police  association  claimed his remarks were wholly  irresponsible  and that the video circulating doesn't  capture all the  intricacies of what took place  but what followed was undoubtedly  outrage  during the unrest one officer appears to  be hit with a brick  what happened oh he just got break  after the shooting the police department  said they had been responding to a  domestic incident  but provided no further details the  officers involved who were yet to be  identified  have been placed on administrative leave  cordelia lynch  sky news

